# Hugo layouts and templates

Site overrides live in root `layouts/`, `assets/`, and `static/` — prefer these over editing `themes/hugo-theme-bootstrap/`. If you must touch the vendored theme, keep the diff minimal.

## After template or asset changes

Run a local Hugo build so failures surface before push:

```bash
hugo server -D          # iteration
hugo --minify --environment production   # production parity
```

Or Docker Compose / commands in `README.md` (Hugo version from `.env`). Pull requests also run the production Docker build via `.github/workflows/hugo-build.yml`.

## SEO partials

`layouts/partials/head.html` is a thin orchestrator; put new `<head>` concerns in a focused partial under `layouts/partials/head/` and wire it from the orchestrator (structure table in `README.md`). Do not add inline meta/SEO markup to `head.html`.

- Document `<title>`: `layouts/partials/head/title.html` (called from `baseof.html`; home falls back to `Site.Title`).
- Keywords / meta description / fediverse creator: `layouts/partials/head/meta-tags.html`.
- List/archive meta descriptions: `layouts/partials/head/list-page-description.html` (per-page copy targeting 110–160 characters; optional front-matter `description` override; pagination suffix on page 2+).
- Canonical URL: `layouts/partials/head/canonical.html` (called from `head.html`).
- Paginated list `noindex`: `layouts/partials/head/meta/robots.html` + `params.listPaginationMetaRobots` in `config/_default/config.toml` (via theme `head/meta`).
- Search index meta: `layouts/partials/head/search-index.html` (search page only).
- Open Graph / Twitter cards: `layouts/partials/head/seo.html` (Hugo internal templates).
- JSON-LD: `layouts/partials/head/structured-data.html` dispatches to the schema partials (`head/schema-blog-posting.html`, `head/schema-collection-page.html`).
- New external hosts, share imagery, or scripts must stay coherent with CSP, response headers, and `staticwebapp.config.json`.

## Images in templates

HTML partials and shortcodes that emit `<img>` need appropriate `alt` (or equivalent ARIA).
